From: Spaceghost <spaceghost@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] lib: provide bcmp for LLVM memcmp folding

LLVM can fold equality-only memcmp calls to bcmp even in this older
freestanding kernel. Provide the equivalent internal implementation.

---
 lib/string.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/lib/string.c b/lib/string.c
--- a/lib/string.c
+++ b/lib/string.c
@@ -1041,1 +1041,7 @@
 #endif	/* CONFIG_STRING_SELFTEST */
+
+int bcmp(const void *left, const void *right, size_t len)
+{
+	return memcmp(left, right, len);
+}
+EXPORT_SYMBOL(bcmp);
-- 
